       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Amlodipine 20 mg daily is double the FDA-labeled maximum of 10 mg once daily. Doses above 10 mg raise the risk of hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema, and they usually add little blood pressure control.\n\nPlease tell me which of these you want:\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the maximum standard dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written.** If you're intentionally going above the labeled maximum, tell me and I'll enter it with a note recording that.\n3. **A different regimen.** If 10 mg isn't enough, you could add a second agent such as an ARB, ACE inhibitor, or thiazide-like diuretic.\n\nIf I misread the dose, for example if you meant 2.5 mg or 5 mg, tell me the correct dose and I'll enter it."
      }
